  "category": "metabolic",
  "topic": "metabolism",
  "summary": "Fatty acids are activated to acyl-CoA, carried into mitochondria by the carnitine shuttle, and shortened two carbons per round by four reactions (oxidation, hydration, oxidation, thiolysis). Palmitate (C16) needs 7 rounds and yields 8 acetyl-CoA.",
  "evidence": "established",
  "layout": "cycle",
  "location": "Mitochondrial matrix (very-long-chain FAs start in peroxisomes)",
  "net": "Palmitoyl-CoA + 7 FAD + 7 NAD⁺ + 7 CoA + 7 H₂O → 8 Acetyl-CoA + 7 FADH₂ + 7 NADH + 7 H⁺",
  "clinical": "MCAD deficiency (the most common FAO disorder) causes hypoketotic hypoglycaemia during fasting and is included in newborn screening. CPT1 is inhibited by malonyl-CoA, preventing simultaneous synthesis and oxidation.",
